<p dir="ltr">A realistic budget covers far more than visible finishes. Structural and <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/interior-architecture/">interior architecture</a> work, mechanical and electrical upgrades, bespoke cabinetry, <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/procurement/">procurement</a> of furniture and fittings, project management, and contingency (usually 10–15% of the build cost) all need to be priced in from the outset. Factoring in <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/how-much-does-bespoke-joinery-cost-in-london-in-2026/">how much bespoke joinery costs in London</a> helps ensure millwork and fitted wardrobes are budgeted accurately rather than estimated as an afterthought.</p>

<h3 dir="ltr">Why Do High-End Renovations Cost More in London Than Elsewhere in the UK?</h3>
<img class="wp-image-11671 size-full" src="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/family-home-interior-designed-by-oraanj-interior-designers.jpeg" alt="" width="1536" height="1024" />
<p dir="ltr">Labour rates in London typically run 20–30% above the national average, and that gap widens further for specialist trades, master joiners, stonemasons, and heritage plasterers are in short supply and priced accordingly. Add to that higher material delivery costs, tighter site access on period terraces, and stricter conservation area or listed building requirements, and London projects consistently outprice the same specification elsewhere in the country. Even in outer London enclaves, managing <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/ruislip/">Ruislip home renovation and design build</a> works requires experienced logistics to maintain budget integrity.</p>

